{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassLeftMulEndomorphism","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassLeftMulEndomorphism","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.End"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_injective","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassLeftMulEndomorphism.lean#L72-L80","doc":"**Faithfulness.**  The regular representation `a ↦ L_a` is injective, so the\nHecke mass element is *faithfully* realised as a module endomorphism — the\nname \"mass endomorphism\" is honest under this identification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassLeftMulEndomorphism.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Evaluating the endomorphism at `1` recovers the element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul_apply","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassLeftMulEndomorphism.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.massLeftMul","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/MassLeftMulEndomorphism.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**The mass element as a genuine endomorphism.**  Left multiplication by\n`a : A` (in particular by the Hecke mass element `Φ_mass(β)`) is a module\nendomorphism `A → A`.  This is the object the chapter calls \"the mass\nendomorphism\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}